  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5286",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to HDLM-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18, and this pathway leads to HDLM-2. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also shown to target Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets HDLM-2. These findings indicate that Mollicellin N may act through different pathways to influence HDLM-2, possibly through distinct molecular mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Mollicellin N and HDLM-2, with the potential for multiple layers of interaction. The evidence supports the idea that Mollicellin N may exert its effects on HDLM-2 through various intermediate targets, underscoring the importance of understanding these interactions for potential therapeutic applications.",
